const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"Shiller比较股票价格波动与之后股利变化所能解释的范围，讨论价格波动的含义。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Do Stock Prices Move Too Much to be Justified by Subsequent Changes in Dividends?” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1257/aer.71.3.421",label:{zh:"American Economic Review (1981) · 来源说明",en:"American Economic Review (1981) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"公开描述将价格与事后股利路径放在现值关系下比较，问题依赖贴现、预期和样本定义。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Do Stock Prices Move Too Much to be Justified by Subsequent Changes in Dividends?”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1257/aer.71.3.421",label:{zh:"American Economic Review (1981) · 来源说明",en:"American Economic Review (1981) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要明确价格、股利、通胀调整、贴现率、观测频率和事后可见信息与当时预期之间的区别。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Do Stock Prices Move Too Much to be Justified by Subsequent Changes in Dividends?”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1257/aer.71.3.421",label:{zh:"American Economic Review (1981) · 来源说明",en:"American Economic Review (1981) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"文章提出价格波动与后续股利解释之间的张力，而非提供一个可以逐日交易的价格偏离指标。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Do Stock Prices Move Too Much to be Justified by Subsequent Changes in Dividends?”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1257/aer.71.3.421",label:{zh:"American Economic Review (1981) · 来源说明",en:"American Economic Review (1981) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"复核现值恒等式、样本起止、股利口径和任何平稳性或预期假设，避免把事后路径当作实时信号。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Do Stock Prices Move Too Much to be Justified by Subsequent Changes in Dividends?”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1257/aer.71.3.421",label:{zh:"American Economic Review (1981) · 来源说明",en:"American Economic Review (1981) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 American Economic Review (1981)。价格与股利关系的长期研究不免除对风险溢价、结构变化和数据修订的单独处理。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites American Economic Review (1981) for “Do Stock Prices Move Too Much to be Justified by Subsequent Changes in Dividends?”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1257/aer.71.3.421",label:{zh:"American Economic Review (1981) · 来源说明",en:"American Economic Review (1981) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Do Stock Prices Move Too Much to be Justified by Subsequent Changes in Dividends?”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。价格与股利关系的长期研究不免除对风险溢价、结构变化和数据修订的单独处理。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Do Stock Prices Move Too Much to be Justified by Subsequent Changes in Dividends?”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
